8AAAABQ3ej7A","user":{"login":"GDevSh007","id":247660653,"node_id":"U_kgDODsMAbQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247660653?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GDevSh007","html_url":"https://github.com/GDevSh007","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GDevSh007/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GDevSh007/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GDevSh007/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GDevSh007/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GDevSh007/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GDevSh007/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GDevSh007/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GDevSh007/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GDevSh007/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-26T14:33:41Z","updated_at":"2026-08-26T14:38:44Z","body":"> Could it maybe be related to this? https://community.khronos.org/t/out-var-of-vertex-shader-disconnected-from-in-var-of-fragment-shader/106958/4 If you lower \"rendering/limits/global_shader_variables/buffer_size\" to something like 2000 in the MRP does it still occur?\n\nI don't have knowledge of graphics drivers related things like UBO and SSBO as being discussed in thread of the provided link! But I did tried your suggestions regarding the shader buffer limit changes! Tried different values both below 2000 and above the default 65k but that didn't solve it! Then I had my eyes on 'Rendering/GL Compatibility/Item Buffer Size' and I increased its value to 50k which seemed to solved the glitch! But only in the 2D editor space! Glitch still appears on play runtime! One more thing that I noticed is that glitch doesn't occur on running the scenes independently but only when it is instantiated as packed scene!\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/059b49ee-e840-4d6e-a4dd-7a6dd14f3d3f\n\nAdditionally! Here is graphics driver related console log:\n\nGodot Engine v4.8.dev2.official.7220d456d - https://godotengine.org\nOpenGL API OpenGL ES 3.2 V@0502.0 (GIT@db3d445dbc, Ia06b22fa1a, 1633355031) (Date:10/04/21) - Compatibility - Using Device: Qualcomm - Adreno (TM) 650\n\n--- Debugging process stopped ---\n\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5426881516/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5427214479","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122741#issuecomment-5427214479","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122741","id":5427214479,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQ3y4jw","user":{"login":"GDevSh007","id":247660653,"node_id":"U_kgDODsMAbQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247660653?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GDevSh007","html_url":"https://github.com/GDevSh007","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GDevSh007/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GDevSh007/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GDevSh007/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GDevSh007/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GDevSh007/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GDevSh007/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GDevSh007/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GDevSh007/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GDevSh007/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-26T14:59:22Z","updated_at":"2026-08-26T17:23:50Z","body":"@skorpnok  Also check out this search result if it might be useful!\n\n<img width=\"1080\" height=\"5417\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5ee2251a-8ca7-4e41-a4f6-ea99adb960fd\" />","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5427214479/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"low-quality"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5427944972","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122741#issuecomment-5427944972","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122741","id":5427944972,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQ4feDA","user":{"login":"skorpnok","id":6632336,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MzIzMzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6632336?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok","html_url":"https://github.com/skorpnok","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-26T16:19:21Z","updated_at":"2026-08-26T16:23:21Z","body":"My suspicion is that the adreno drivers for GLES3 are finicky (as in extremely low limits and or buggy) as is discussed in that forum thread. What I think is happening is that the driver may not allocate the full UBO size that Godot is asking for but silently allocates less. The extra uniforms are then in \"random\" memory where other stuff can write over them. Most (if not all?) mobile gpu's do something called tiled rendering, which might explain the checkered pattern (not sure what the tile size is) as different tiles read different values since other stuff overwrites them inbetween tiles. I do not think that `item buffer size` is directly related but may just mean that the dangling memory is not getting thrashed by chance. Memory related bugs tend to be very hard to debug. Does lowering `item buffer size` help or just increasing it?\n\nI might also be completely wrong and it's something simple.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5427944972/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5428112021","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122741#issuecomment-5428112021","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122741","id":5428112021,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQ4pqlQ","user":{"login":"GDevSh007","id":247660653,"node_id":"U_kgDODsMAbQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247660653?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GDevSh007","html_url":"https://github.com/GDevSh007","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GDevSh007/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GDevSh007/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GDevSh007/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GDevSh007/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GDevSh007/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GDevSh007/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GDevSh007/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GDevSh007/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GDevSh007/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-26T16:34:32Z","updated_at":"2026-08-26T16:34:32Z","body":"Hmm, we might as well bring the attention of @blueskythlikesclouds  into this issue. Since he's been solving a lots of rendering related issues single handedly ;-) Mentioned by @clayjohn in his presentation at the Godot Con, Boston.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5428112021/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5428161253","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122741#issuecomment-5428161253","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122741","id":5428161253,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQ4sq5Q","user":{"login":"GDevSh007","id":247660653,"node_id":"U_kgDODsMAbQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247660653?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GDevSh007","html_url":"https://github.com/GDevSh007","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GDevSh007/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GDevSh007/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GDevSh007/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GDevSh007/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GDevSh007/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GDevSh007/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GDevSh007/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GDevSh007/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GDevSh007/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-26T16:38:56Z","updated_at":"2026-08-26T16:38:56Z","body":"> My suspicion is that the adreno drivers for GLES3 are finicky (as in extremely low limits and or buggy) as is discussed in that forum thread. What I think is happening is that the driver may not allocate the full UBO size that Godot is asking for but silently allocates less. The extra uniforms are then in \"random\" memory where other stuff can write over them. Most (if not all?) mobile gpu's do something called tiled rendering, which might explain the checkered pattern (not sure what the tile size is) as different tiles read different values since other stuff overwrites them inbetween tiles. I do not think that `item buffer size` is directly related but may just mean that the dangling memory is not getting thrashed by chance. Memory related bugs tend to be very hard to debug. Does lowering `item buffer size` help or just increasing it?\n> \n> I might also be completely wrong and it's something simple.\n\nI tried increasing it! It solved for once then I couldn't see the glitch appearing even after reverting the value to default! So not sure how it worked!","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5428161253/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]